The example meeting (ui/example/fr, ui/example/en) is an invented meeting of two voices, made by
scripts/example.py with the Piper speech synthesiser. No real meeting and no real person are in it.
Its voices are Piper voice models, each trained on a public speech corpus:

French, both voices: fr_FR-mls-medium, speakers 3698 and 1840.
  Voice model: https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/raw/main/fr/fr_FR/mls/medium/MODEL_CARD
  Corpus: Multilingual LibriSpeech (MLS), French, by Vineel Pratap, Qiantong Xu, Anuroop Sriram,
  Gabriel Synnaeve and Ronan Collobert, https://openslr.org/94/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

English, « Vous »: en_US-joe-medium.
  Voice model: https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/raw/main/en/en_US/joe/medium/MODEL_CARD
  Corpus: https://github.com/OHF-Voice/voice-datasets
  Licence: CC0 1.0 Universal, public domain, https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

English, « Les autres »: en_GB-cori-medium.
  Voice model: https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/raw/main/en/en_GB/cori/medium/MODEL_CARD
  Corpus: Hi-Fi Multi-Speaker English TTS (Hi-Fi TTS), by Evelina Bakhturina, Vitaly Lavrukhin,
  Boris Ginsburg and Yang Zhang, NVIDIA, https://www.openslr.org/109/
  Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: the voices speak sentences written for Kitokey; their sound is resampled to 16,000
samples a second and kept as FLAC. The corpora and voice models are provided as is, without
warranty of any kind.
